# Multi-root ("Brick-of-Roots") adaptive trees

This directory provides a drop-in extension of Basilisk's `quadtree.h` and
`octree.h` grids supporting non-cubic domains via `dimensions(nx, ny, nz)` —
a rectangular brick of $n_x \times n_y \times n_z$ root cells, with full
adaptive mesh refinement, periodicity, dump/restore, and MPI load balancing.

## Usage

Include the grid header from this sandbox (with `BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH`
pointing to `sandbox/`):

~~~literatec
#include "acastillo/grid/quadtree.h"  // 2D
#include "acastillo/grid/octree.h"    // 3D
~~~

Then set the domain aspect ratio with `dimensions(nx, ny)` (2D) or
`dimensions(nx, ny, nz)` (3D) before `init_grid(N)` (where `N` is a multiple
of `nx` by a power of two).

## Summary of changes vs. `$BASILISK/src/grid/`

* [quadtree.h](quadtree.h), [octree.h](octree.h): Unchanged entry points
  (byte-identical to upstream) so relative includes resolve locally.
* [memindex/virtual.h](memindex/virtual.h): Generalizes the sparse virtual
  array size from scalar `int len` to per-axis `ivec len` for rectangular
  bricks (`nx != ny != nz`), and fixes the `mem_free1d` slice bound.
* [foreach_cell.h](foreach_cell.h): Adds `for_each_root()` and extends
  `foreach_cell*` / `foreach_cell_restore` to traverse all
  $n_x \times n_y \times n_z$ roots while avoiding periodic alias
  double-visits.
* [tree.h](tree.h): Adds `dimensions(nx, ny, nz)`, `Dimensions_scale` /
  `_DELTA`, per-axis `Layer.len`, multi-root `init_grid()`, `periodic_function`,
  `locate()`, `tree_is_full()`, `tree_periodic()`, 1D/2D/3D periodic-aware
  `check_two_one()`, and independent `(kx, ky)` corner loops in
  `diagonal_neighbor_2D()` for `BGHOSTS >= 2` at level 0.
* [tree-common.h](tree-common.h): Generalizes `periodic_clamp()` to per-axis
  extents and handles `refine_level(0)` MPI updates.
* [tree-mpi.h](tree-mpi.h): Adds level-0 inter-root halo exchange,
  `sync_root_pids()`, multi-root `restore_mpi()`, and root-prefix-sum
  `z_weights()` / `z_indexing()`.
* [balance.h](balance.h): Migrates level-0 root $5^d$ neighborhoods,
  synchronizes root and prolongation-child `pid`s before rebuilding halo
  buffers, and updates `grid->tn` / `grid->maxdepth` for `npe() == 1`.

---

# Multi-GPU (`CUDA + MPI`), Rectangular Sub-Brick MPI & FP64 GPU Multigrid

This directory also provides:

1. **Double- and single-precision GPU multigrid backends** for both **CUDA**
   (`libbuda64.a`, `libbuda.a`) and **OpenGL/GLSL** (`libgpu64.a`, `libgpu.a`)
   in 2D and 3D.
2. **Multi-GPU (`CUDA + MPI`) and arbitrary-rank rectangular sub-brick MPI
   multigrid** (`LocalDims`), removing upstream `multigrid-mpi.h`'s
   `npe = nx*ny*nz * (2^d)^i` single-root-per-rank restriction on both CUDA
   GPUs and CPUs, with CUDA-aware MPI (GPUDirect P2P / RDMA) and automatic
   pinned-host fallback (`BASILISK_CUDA_MPI=0|1`).

## Building the runtime libraries

Build the static libraries once inside `sandbox/acastillo/grid/` (`libbuda*.a`
are pure CUDA with zero `mpi.h` dependency, so a single build serves both
serial and MPI runs):

~~~bash
make -C $BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH/acastillo/grid/cuda all
make -C $BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH/acastillo/grid/gpu all
~~~

## Usage

Include the desired backend header (with `BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH` pointing to
`sandbox/`), and compile with either `CC=gcc` (1 GPU / 1 CPU) or
`CC='mpicc -D_MPI=N'` ($N$ GPUs or $N$ CPU ranks):

~~~literatec
#include "acastillo/grid/cuda/multigrid_fp64.h"    // 2D CUDA FP64 (1 or N GPUs)
#include "acastillo/grid/cuda/multigrid3D_fp64.h"  // 3D CUDA FP64 (1 or N GPUs)
#include "acastillo/grid/cuda/multigrid.h"         // 2D CUDA FP32 (1 or N GPUs)
#include "acastillo/grid/cuda/multigrid3D.h"       // 3D CUDA FP32 (1 or N GPUs)
#include "acastillo/grid/gpu/multigrid_fp64.h"     // 2D OpenGL FP64
#include "acastillo/grid/gpu/multigrid3D_fp64.h"   // 3D OpenGL FP64
#include "acastillo/grid/multigrid.h"              // 2D CPU / rectangular MPI
#include "acastillo/grid/multigrid3D.h"            // 3D CPU / rectangular MPI
~~~

By default under `_MPI`, `mpi_boundary_new()` automatically factors `npe()`
into `MpiDims = {px, py, pz}` to preserve the coarsest root grid (`S = 1` when
`p_d | nx_d`) and minimize halo surface area; an explicit decomposition can
also be requested via `mpi_dims(px, py, pz)` before `init_grid()`. For
canonical multi-root `dump()` / `restore()` and 3D `output_ppm_slice()`, see
[`acastillo/output_fields/dump_restore.h`](../output_fields/dump_restore.h) and
[`acastillo/output_fields/output_ppm_slice.h`](../output_fields/output_ppm_slice.h).

## Summary of changes vs. `$BASILISK/src/grid/`

* [multigrid.h](multigrid.h), [multigrid1D.h](multigrid1D.h),
  [multigrid3D.h](multigrid3D.h): Introduces `UserDims`, `MpiDims`, `LocalDims`,
  `mpi_dims()`, and `global_root_index()`, unifies `_ND()`, `SET_DIMENSIONS()`,
  and `locate()` across serial and MPI, skips internal MPI seam faces in
  `box_boundary_level()`, and defines `foreach_cell()` over `LocalDims`.
* [multigrid-mpi.h](multigrid-mpi.h): Adds rectangular sub-brick factorization,
  pointer-keyed MPI `+` reduction helpers, `foreach_dimension()` CPU halo
  slices, canonical `for_each_root (LocalDims)` `z_indexing()`, and the
  batched GPU-resident `mpi_boundary_level_gpu()` halo exchange.
* [gpu-multigrid.h](gpu-multigrid.h): Derives `SINGLE_PRECISION` /
  `DOUBLE_PRECISION` cleanly, includes `multigrid-mpi.h` under `_MPI`, and
  syncs `subtree_size()` to host when read on CPU.
* [gpu/gpu.h](gpu/gpu.h): Merges `listf` into `listc` under `_MPI` to prevent
  rank divergence on wall-normal face BCs, enables host-synced `foreach_region`
  on `_CUDA`, and dispatches GPU-resident fields to `mpi_boundary_level_gpu()`.
* [gpu/grid.h](gpu/grid.h): Adds `dvec2`/`dvec3` and native FP64 device math,
  64-bit `size_t` `_CUDA` SSBO indexing (`> 4G` elements), non-divisor
  `LocalDims` workgroup sizing, `_mpi_wall` physical-BC mask, `_mpi_seam` face
  reduction mask, lazy per-level `s_phys_gpu` / `mpi_clean` halo schedule,
  `MPI_Allreduce` on GPU reductions, `ferr`/`fout` external filtering, and
  opt-in `-DSTRICT_GPU=1`.
* [cuda/cuda.c](cuda/cuda.c): Adds FP64 support (`typedef double real`,
  `reset_scalar`, `cuda_reduce`, non-divisor register block clamping), local
  MPI rank GPU binding (`cuda_set_device`), `dlsym("MPIX_Query_cuda_support")`
  detection (keeping `libbuda{,64}.a` `mpi.h`-free), atomic PID-suffixed NVRTC
  PTX caching, FP32 subnormal literal clamping (`1e-50f`), sub-brick
  `foreach_point` offsets, and GPU `halo_pack` / `halo_unpack` kernels.
* [gpu/opengl.c](gpu/opengl.c), [gpu/reduction.c](gpu/reduction.c): Adds FP64
  support and fixes non-square `Dimensions` scratch-SSBO sizing and
  `foreach_point` offsets in OpenGL reductions.
* [cuda/Makefile](cuda/Makefile), [gpu/Makefile](gpu/Makefile), and
  `{cuda,gpu}/multigrid*.h`: Build and autolink `libbuda{,64}.a` (`-ldl`) and
  `libgpu{,64}.a` via `$BASILISK_INCLUDE_PATH/acastillo/grid/{cuda,gpu}`.
